KZ3 patch 1072 (SPU pass 57): KZ3_JOIN2_PROBE=1, logs only (off: one NULL function-pointer test per rdch/rchcnt).
The T7 quit-to-menu stalls in cellSpursJoinTask2 called from the Havok pool destructor (the RE notes s.7).
spu_workload.c keeps a registry of live taskset task threads (taskset, id, generation, image, start time, the SPU
context seen by rdch/rchcnt, per-channel read/count calls) and a ring of the last task starts/exits (exit of a
cut-off task marked), and spu_j2_dump prints them with the taskset's ready/pending/enabled bitsets, the Taskset2 size
word, exit entries and task_info of ids 0..7; cellSpursJoinTask2 calls it at ~3, ~20 and ~40 s of spinning, plus the
port's guest dump hook g_kz3_j2_guest_dump.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): both (stop request, then the join2 note).

